  "presentation_summary": [
    "49-year-old HIV-infected man on antiretroviral therapy had virological suppression but poor immune response with CD4 count 95 cells/mm3.",
    "Initial evaluation showed pancytopenia, rouleaux, mildly elevated ferritin, and mild splenomegaly 14.3 cm; he lacked typical fever.",
    "He had chronic abdominal pain, fullness, intermittent diarrhea and constipation, nausea, and vomiting; endoscopic biopsies showed gastrointestinal leishmaniasis.",
    "Bone marrow aspirate confirmed Leishmania amastigotes and he received liposomal amphotericin B, with partial hematologic and spleen-size improvement.",
    "One year later repeat bone marrow aspirate confirmed VL relapse; PCR speciated Leishmania donovani, and relapse was treated with liposomal amphotericin B plus miltefosine."
  ],
